To compute

$$
\begin{aligned}

		\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  &\operatorname{div}   \dfrac {2a} {14b^2},
	\end{aligned}
$$

we just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:

$$
\begin{aligned}\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  \operatorname{div}   \dfrac {2a} {14b^2} &= \dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  \cdot \dfrac {14b^2} {2a} \\ &= \dfrac {2a(a^2 - 5)} {7b}  \cdot  \dfrac {2b \cdot 7b} {2a} \\ &= \dfrac {\cancel{2a}(a^2 - 5)} {\cancel{7b}}  \cdot  \dfrac {2b \cdot \cancel{7b}} {\cancel{2a}} \\ &= \dfrac {2b(a^2 - 5)} 1 \\ &= 2a^2b - 10b\end{aligned}
$$

